  "question": {
    "text": "The number of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi></math>&nbsp;electrons in the ground state electronic configuration of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Gd</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math> is [Atomic number of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Gd</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>64</mn><mo>]</mo></math>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "7",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Electronic configuration of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Gd</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>[</mo><mi>Xe</mi><mo>]</mo><mn>4</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi><mn>7</mn></msup><mn>5</mn><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi></mrow><mn>1</mn></msup><mn>6</mn><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></math></p><p>Due to&nbsp;more stable exactly half-filled&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi><mn>7</mn></msup></math>&nbsp;shell, electron filling occur in a little higher energy <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mo>-</mo></math>orbital</p><p>So configuration of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Gd</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mo>[</mo><mi>Xe</mi><mo>]</mo><mn>4</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi><mn>7</mn></msup><mn>5</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></math>&nbsp;</p>",
